      "value": "@{5e77efb6d430414fec89bb86|full_name}But this isnt to do with them having the system or not, make anotehr post if you want to post about that.\n\nThis post is about those who already DO use the current stystem.\n\nYea many people would rather just straight pay with normal money, and using their own system is more predatory to customers, but this post isnt about that, and that is unrelated. This is for those who are using the system to have a clearer way of checking how much their currentsy is worth before they cash out.\n\nFor example, I myself have about 109,000 \\V,  but its hard to know how much that translates to in $, and if I only wanted to cashout when it reaches a certain $ ammount, its hard to know. I know its roughly $500, but i dont know exactly how much. It can also mean If I was in need of money for something, I could just cash out the exact amount I need. Lots of creators use the marketplace as income to pay rent and for food and stuff, so its IMPORTANT to be able to know what we have on our accounts, espeshally as you can only cashout once every 2 weeks \n\nIm not discussing whether or not we should have \\V, I'm suggesting a clearer way for those who have earned (not bought) \\V to translate into the currency they cash out into. Tilla isn't clear on it either unless you are physically on the cashout page.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
